% productivity.ill — till executable spec: positive delay = guardedness (D16, E2).
%
% STATUS: written ahead of the engine (TDD) — see schedule.ill header.
% Ground truth: tests/engine/till-oracle.test.js ("in-flight atomicity and productivity").
%
% A self-loop with delay 1 is PRODUCTIVE: each firing advances logical time
% (events at 0,1,2,3 under settle 3; the token ends at stamp 4). The same rule
% with @0 is a Zeno cycle — settle diverges at the instant and must be caught
% by the maxSteps guard (negative test lives in the JS oracle suite; .ill tests
% stay positive).

ping: a -o { a }@1.

#expect_productive (settle: 3)
  a
  =>
  a@4 .

#expect_not_stuck_at_zero (settle: 3)
  a
  =>
  a@0 .
